{"event": "tool_result", "turn": 1, "payload": {"tool_name": "get_tool_schema", "success": true, "summary": "Schema for **create_app**:\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"create_app\",\n  \"description\": \"Create a new application end-to-end. Writes BOTH the security registration AND the UI-side application override doc in one call \\u2014 both are required for the app to be usable; the security row alone leaves the app invisible (every /api/ui/* read 403s).\\n\\nRequired: `app_code` \\u2014 letters only (no digits, no underscores, no dashes \\u2014 the platform enforces `onlyAlphabetAllowed`).\\n\\n**Important platform rule:** the UI document's `name` MUST equal `app_code` exactly. The `name` parameter is accepted for compatibility but always overridden to match `app_code` \\u2014 you cannot give the app a separate display name through this tool. If you want a display label, set it via translations later.\\n\\nOptional but important:\\n- `default_page` \\u2014 the page name to set as `properties.defaultPage`. The app needs a defaultPage to be browser-reachable; pass this if you already know which page will be the landing one. Otherwise, create your first page next, then call `update_app` (or `set_app_page_reference`) to set it.\\n- `app_type` \\u2014 APP (default-routing) | SITE (the common one, default) | POSTER.\\n- `app_access_type` \\u2014 OWN (only the creating client, default) | ANY (every tenant) | EXPLICIT (requires `grant_app_access` per client).\\n\\nTwo-step flow this tool runs:\\n1. POST /api/security/applications \\u2014 registers the app in the security DB so subsequent writes pass authorization.\\n2. POST /api/ui/applications \\u2014 writes the UI override doc (properties / languages / translations). Without this, GET on the app returns 403 even though the security row exists.\\n\\nAfter this tool succeeds, the typical next moves are:\\n- `create_page(name=\\\"home\\\", ...)` \\u2014 your landing page.\\n- If you didn't pass `default_page`, `update_app(app_code=..., properties={\\\"defaultPage\\\": \\\"home\\\"})` \\u2014 wires the app's entry route.\",\n  \"input_schema\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"app_code\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"Unique appCode (letters ONLY \\u2014 no digits, no underscores, no dashes \\u2014 used in URLs and security checks)\"\n      },\n      \"name\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"Accepted but always overridden to equal app_code (platform requirement). Pass app_code or omit.\"\n      },\n      \"default_page\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"Page name to set as properties.defaultPage. Convenience \\u2014 equivalent to setting it via `properties` later. The page itself doesn't need to exist yet; create it next and the routing links up.\"\n      },\n      \"app_type\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"APP | SITE | POSTER. SITE is the usual choice for a customer-facing app.\",\n        \"default\": \"SITE\"\n      },\n      \"app_access_type\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"OWN | ANY | EXPLICIT. OWN restricts to the creating client.\",\n        \"default\": \"OWN\"\n      },\n      \"client_code\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"Owning clientCode for the UI doc (defaults to session)\"\n      },\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"description\": \"UI app properties: defaultPage, loginPage, shellPage, forbiddenPage, notFoundPage, signUp, etc. Top-level field names, NOT wrapped in {value:...}.\"\n      },\n      \"languages\": {\n        \"type\": \"array\",\n        \"description\": \"Supported locale codes, e.g. ['en','hi','ar']\"\n      },\n      \"translations\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"description\": \"Translation map: {locale: {translationKey: translatedString}}\"\n      },\n      \"thumb_url\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"Thumbnail URL stored on the security app record\"\n      },\n      \"message\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"Commit message\",\n        \"default\": \"Created via CFA\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"required\": [\n      \"app_code\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```", "tool_use_id": "call_00_rbeyGyrzmj8vUrEP7M1L9031", "agent_id": "appbuilder"}}
